// GENERATED by scripts/fetchPokemonSetCodes.cjs — do not edit by hand.
//
// CF-THE-SET-CODE-IS-THE-KEY (2026-09-05). Sellers write the set CODE as often
// as the set NAME — "SVP EN-SV Black Star", "Japanese M5-Abyss Eye", "SWSH12.5"
// — and the name-keyed table (pokemonSetAliases.ts) cannot see any of them.
// The unknown-setKey census (#1796) measured the cost: the Pokemon half of the
// ~500k "needs vocabulary" bucket is overwhelmingly promo and code spellings.
//
// Source: api.tcgdex.net (MIT). 218 English sets, 184 Japanese, read
// 2026-09-05. Codes are slugified — tcgdex writes `sv08.5`, the
// catalog is keyed `sv08-5`.
//
// THE VALUE IS THE SET NAME, AND IT IS DOCUMENTATION, NOT A KEY. The KEY of
// each record is the canonical setKey; the value is what tcgdex calls that set,
// kept so a reader can tell `me02` from `me02-5` without a second lookup.
//
// AMBIGUOUS CODES ARE NOT IN THE JA MAP, and that omission is the load-bearing
// part. 24 ids exist in BOTH markets naming DIFFERENT products:
//
//   neo1   EN "Neo Genesis" vs JA "金、銀、新世界へ..."
//   neo2   EN "Neo Discovery" vs JA "遺跡をこえて..."
//   neo3   EN "Neo Revelation" vs JA "めざめる伝説"
//   neo4   EN "Neo Destiny" vs JA "闇、そして光へ..."
//   sm1    EN "Sun & Moon" vs JA "サン＆ムーン"
//   sm10   EN "Unbroken Bonds" vs JA "ダブルブレイズ"
//   sm11   EN "Unified Minds" vs JA "ミラクルツイン"
//   sm12   EN "Cosmic Eclipse" vs JA "オルタージェネシス"
//   sm2    EN "Guardians Rising" vs JA "新たなる試練の向こう"
//   sm3    EN "Burning Shadows" vs JA "ひかる伝説"
//   sm4    EN "Crimson Invasion" vs JA "GXバトルブースト"
//   sm5    EN "Ultra Prism" vs JA "ウルトラフォース"
//   sm6    EN "Forbidden Light" vs JA "禁断の光"
//   sm7    EN "Celestial Storm" vs JA "裂空のカリスマ"
//   sm8    EN "Lost Thunder" vs JA "超爆インパクト"
//   sm9    EN "Team Up" vs JA "タッグボルト"
//   sv10   EN "Destined Rivals" vs JA "ロケット団の栄光"
//   xy10   EN "Fates Collide" vs JA "めざめる超王"
//   xy2    EN "Flashfire" vs JA "ワイルドブレイズ"
//   xy3    EN "Furious Fists" vs JA "ライジングフィスト"
//   xy4    EN "Phantom Forces" vs JA "ファントムゲート"
//   xy6    EN "Roaring Skies" vs JA "エメラルドブレイク"
//   xy7    EN "Ancient Origins" vs JA "バンデットリング"
//   xy9    EN "BREAKpoint" vs JA "破天の怒り"
//
// A bare `sm1` in a title says nothing about which of those two cards it is,
// and they are different prints with different markets and different prices.
// So they are keyed ENGLISH (which is what the English branch already answers)
// and the Japanese products are reached by NAME through
// japanesePokemonAliases.ts — the same rule CF-THE-JAPANESE-CODE-IS-THE-KEY
// states, applied to codes.

